 ${camlab:Depends}
# camlab-setup installs drivers after kernel.sh prunes the
# sibling kernel flavor.
Suggests: ar0234-rpi-dkms,
 ar0822-rpi-dkms,
 imx585-rpi-dkms
Description: Kiosk app for live preview and testing MIPI CSI camera modules
 Runs on Raspberry Pi 5 and CM5. Sensor and CSI port are chosen in the GUI.
 Covers AR0234, AR0822, IMX283, IMX462, IMX477 and IMX585.
 .
 Viewfinder carries focus peaking, zebra clipping, histogram and focus map.
 Exposure, gain and white balance run auto or manual. Resolution, bit depth
 and frame rate come from sensor modes. Drives a DSI touch panel, HDMI
 monitor or both at once.
 .
 Camera and kernel driver errors surface in a log panel, which separates
 a bad overlay from bad wiring. App, camera stack and sensor drivers update
 from the Kurokesu apt archive without leaving the GUI.
